%META:TOPICPARENT{name="WebHome"}%
---+ Keyboard Shortcuts

%TOC%

All shortcuts are single-press unless =Shift= is noted. Typing into a
text field (threshold input, event search, background hex input)
suppresses the hotkeys until focus leaves the field. Combinations with
=Ctrl=, =Cmd= or =Alt= are reserved for the browser.

The =Esc= key is overloaded by a small priority chain that closes
whichever overlay is on top of the stack.

---++ Camera and view

| *Key*       | *Action*                                            |
| Mouse drag  | Orbit camera                                        |
| Scroll      | Zoom                                                |
| Right-drag  | Pan                                                 |
| =R=         | Reset view to the default isometric                 |

---++ Panels and dialogs

| *Key*    | *Action*                                              |
| =M=      | Pin / unpin the left (data-source) panel              |
| =E=      | Pin / unpin the right (energy threshold) panel        |
| =S=      | Open the Settings panel                               |
| =P=      | Open the Screenshot dialog                            |
| =Shift+B= | Open the scene background colour picker              |
| =Esc=    | Clear pinned tooltips, close the topmost overlay      |

The =Esc= priority chain, in order: pinned tooltips (if any) &rarr;
slicer active &rarr; cinema mode &rarr; settings panel &rarr; layers
panel &rarr; right panel pinned &rarr; screenshot dialog &rarr; left
panel pinned &rarr; about overlay. =Esc= only acts on the first item
that is active, so it clears pinned tooltips before touching any panel.

---++ Scene toggles

| *Key*       | *Action*                                                                |
| =T=         | Toggle TILE sub-detector                                                |
| =L= or =A=  | Toggle LAr (EMB + EMEC)                                                 |
| =H=         | Toggle HEC                                                              |
| =F=         | Toggle FCAL                                                             |
| =G=         | Toggle the ATLAS Ghost envelopes                                        |
| =J=         | Toggle reconstructed tracks                                             |
| =K=         | Toggle topological clusters (or, at L3, the Particles popover)          |
| =I=         | Toggle the cell-hover tooltip and outline                               |
| =C=         | Enter or exit cinema mode                                               |
| =Shift+S=   | Toggle the cylindrical-wedge slicer                                     |
| =Shift+M=   | Toggle the &eta; / &phi; minimap                                        |

The =V= "All cells" toggle and the =B= beam-axis toggle are available
via the toolbar; they are not bound to a keyboard shortcut in the
current build.

---++ Cell tooltips

Hovering a cell or reconstructed object shows a floating tooltip (the
=I= key toggles this on or off). With the tooltip enabled it can be
*pinned* so it stays on screen while you inspect or compare several
objects at once:

| *Gesture / key*               | *Effect*                                      |
| Click an object               | Pin its tooltip as a standalone card          |
| Click a pinned object again   | Remove that object's card                     |
| =Esc=                         | Clear every pinned card at once               |

Pinned cards are anchored to their object in 3D, so they follow it as
you orbit, zoom or pan, and hide while the object is behind the camera.
Any number can be pinned at once, and the live hover tooltip keeps
working independently alongside them.

---++ Slicer gestures

When the slicer is active, the 3D handle at the origin accepts these
pointer gestures:

| *Gesture*                  | *Effect*                                                    |
| Left-drag, screen-Y        | Sweep the wedge angle &theta; from 0 to 2&pi;               |
| Left-drag, screen-X        | Scale the cylinder height (symmetric around the anchor)     |
| Right-drag on the handle   | Translate the cut volume in the world (y, z) plane          |

See [[UserInterface#Slicer_cylindrical_wedge][Slicer]] for the full
description.

---++ Minimap gestures

When the minimap is open and the cursor is over the plot:

| *Gesture / key*                          | *Effect*                                       |
| Mousedown + drag on empty area           | Draw a new region rectangle                    |
| Mousedown + drag on existing rectangle   | Translate the rectangle                        |
| Click on existing rectangle              | Delete the rectangle                           |
| Scroll wheel                             | Zoom the &eta; / &phi; viewport                |
| =+= / === / =&minus;= while hovered      | Zoom in / out                                  |
| =0= while hovered                        | Reset the zoom to the full event               |
| Drag the seam slider (left strip)        | Rotate the &phi; cylinder cut                  |
| Double-click the seam slider             | Reset the seam to =&minus;&pi;=                |

See [[Minimap][Minimap]] for the full description.

